  "narration": {
    "pattern_romaji": "A wa B desu ka",
    "pattern_jp": "AはBですか",
    "pattern_english": "Is A B?",
    "slots": [
      {
        "slot": "A",
        "fits": "the topic: a thing, a person, a time word like today or tomorrow, or 'this' (これ)"
      },
      {
        "slot": "B",
        "fits": "a noun you're asking about: weather (あめ, はれ, くもり), a drink (コーヒー, おちゃ), a person's name or job"
      }
    ],
    "segments": [
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Welcome back! Today's pattern is {AはBですか}. It means: Is A B? It's how you ask a yes-or-no question."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "AはBですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Here's the good news: you already know almost all of it. Last time you learned {AはBです}, which means A is B. Today we add just one tiny sound at the very end: {か}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Let's walk through the slots. A is the topic, the thing you're talking about. Then comes {は}, the little word that marks the topic. B is the noun you're asking about. Then {です}, which means 'is'. And last, {か}, which turns everything into a question."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Notice the word order. English moves 'is' to the front to make a question: 'It is rain' becomes 'Is it rain?' Japanese doesn't move anything. The order stays the same, and the question word {か} just goes at the end."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Let's build one. Start with the topic, {今日}, which means today, plus {は}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "今日は"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "As for today. Now add {あめ}, rain, and {です}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "今日はあめです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Today is rainy. That's a statement. Now add {か}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "今日はあめですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Is it rainy today? That's exactly what Ken asks in today's dialogue."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Another one. Start with {これは}, which means 'as for this'."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "これは"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Add {コーヒー}, coffee, and {です}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "これはコーヒーです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "This is coffee. Now finish it with {か}."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "これはコーヒーですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Is this coffee? And to answer, say {はい}, yes, or {いいえ}, no, then the real answer."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "いいえ、おちゃです。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "No, it's tea."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Now a swap. Keep the same skeleton, but use {あした}, tomorrow, and {はれ}, sunny weather."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "B",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "あしたははれですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Will it be sunny tomorrow? Same frame, new words. Put any topic in A and any noun in B."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "Here's a memory trick: think of {か} as a question mark you can hear. Beginners often think they need a rising voice or a different word order. You don't. {か} does the work all by itself."
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "So here's how it snaps onto what you know: any {AはBです} sentence becomes a question when you add {か}. Listen to the pair one more time."
      },
      {
        "kind": "jp",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "おちゃです。おちゃですか。"
      },
      {
        "kind": "en",
        "speaker": "A",
        "speed": "teaching",
        "text": "It's tea. Is it tea? Now let's hear Yuki and Ken use it."
      }
